        "id": "a6f7929d-c07e-4a48-b523-f78f3982dccd"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "9f9aa5a7-de20-4357-8774-398dc115cb28",
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": "# String – properties\r\n\r\nA `String` is a sequence of characters (text) such as `\"John Doe\"`. It is a **class** from `java.lang`, so it is always available without an import.\r\n\r\n**Properties**\r\n- Written inside **double quotes**: `\"Hello\"`. Single quotes are for one `char`: `'H'`.\r\n- **Immutable**: once created, a string can never change. Every method that \"changes\" text (`trim`, `toUpperCase`, `replace`…) returns a **new** string and leaves the original as it was. Always store the result: `name = name.trim();`.\r\n- Every character has an **index** starting at `0`: `\"Java\".charAt(0)` is `'J'`.\r\n- `length()` is a **method** (with brackets). On an array, `length` is a property (no brackets).\r\n- Compare text with **`equals`**, never with `==` (`==` compares object references, not the text).\r\n- `+` joins strings: `\"a\" + \"b\"` → `\"ab\"`. Joining a string with a number turns the number into text: `\"Age: \" + 20` → `\"Age: 20\"`.\r\n- Need to build a long string piece by piece (for example in a loop)? Use `StringBuilder` (last part of this notebook).",
      "metadata": {
        "language": "markdown",
        "id": "9f9aa5a7-de20-4357-8774-398dc115cb28"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "e1600798-684b-4c1e-a528-9c17e567ef73",
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": "//Syntax\r\n//data_type variable_name = \"value\";\r\n\r\n//this is to create a string\r\n// Method: String name = \"...\"\r\n// What:   stores text (a sequence of characters) in a variable; the text goes inside double quotes\r\n// Use:    for names, messages, or any value that is text and not a number\r\nString name = \"John Doe\";\r\nSystem.out.println(\"Name: \" + name); // + joins the label and the variable into one line of text",
      "metadata": {
        "language": "java",
        "id": "e1600798-684b-4c1e-a528-9c17e567ef73",
        "executionSummary": {
          "executionOrder": 2,
          "success": true
        }
      },
      "execution_count": 2,
      "outputs": [
        {
          "output_type": "execute_result",
          "data": {
            "text/plain": "Name: John Doe\r\n"
          },
          "metadata": {},
          "execution_count": 2
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "60019cb6-1c25-4726-97ca-f58c20aae241",
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": "String name = \"John Doe\";\r\nSystem.out.println(\"Name: \" + name);\r\n\r\n//this is to check if a text is inside the string\r\n// Method: contains(text)\r\n// What:   returns true when text appears anywhere inside the string (case matters), otherwise false\r\n// Use:    to search for a word without caring where it is\r\nboolean hasJohn = name.contains(\"John\"); // true, \"John\" is inside \"John Doe\"\r\nSystem.out.println(\"Contains 'John': \" + hasJohn);",
      "metadata": {
        "language": "java",
        "id": "60019cb6-1c25-4726-97ca-f58c20aae241",
        "executionSummary": {
          "executionOrder": 3,
          "success": true
        }
      },
      "execution_count": 3,
      "outputs": [
        {
          "output_type": "execute_result",
          "data": {
            "text/plain": "Name: John Doe\r\nContains 'John': true\r\n"
          },
          "metadata": {},
          "execution_count": 3
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "8fc8876e-9467-4df2-b072-651aad9225d3",
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": "String name = \"My name is John Wick and i worked in a movie called John Wick 4\";\r\nSystem.out.println(\"Name: \" + name);\r\n\r\n//this is to search a longer sentence\r\n// Method: contains(text)\r\n// What:   same as above: true when the text appears anywhere in the string\r\n// Use:    to check that a sentence mentions a word\r\nboolean hasWorked = name.contains(\"worked\"); // true, \"worked\" is inside the sentence\r\nSystem.out.println(\"Contains 'worked': \" + hasWorked);",
      "metadata": {
        "language": "java",
        "id": "8fc8876e-9467-4df2-b072-651aad9225d3",
        "executionSummary": {
          "executionOrder": 6,
          "success": true
        }
      },
      "execution_count": 6,
      "outputs": [
        {
          "output_type": "execute_result",
          "data": {
            "text/plain": "Name: My name is John Wick and i worked in a movie called John Wick 4\r\nContains 'worked': true\r\n"
          },
          "metadata": {},
          "execution_count": 6
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b5a0f6f1-f92c-481e-92dc-8dc089188ca2",
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": "String name = \"My name is John Wick and i worked in a movie called John Wick 4                 \";\r\nSystem.out.println(\"Name: \" + name);\r\n\r\n//this is to remove spaces at the start and end\r\n// Method: trim()\r\n// What:   returns a new string without the leading and trailing spaces; the spaces between words stay\r\n// Use:    to clean up text that came from a user or a file before storing or comparing it\r\nString data = name.trim(); // the 17 spaces after the 4 are removed\r\nSystem.out.println(\"Trimmed: \" + data);\r\nSystem.out.println(\"Length before: \" + name.length() + \", after: \" + data.length());",
      "metadata": {
        "language": "java",
        "id": "b5a0f6f1-f92c-481e-92dc-8dc089188ca2",
        "executionSummary": {
          "executionOrder": 7,
          "success": true
        }
      },
      "execution_count": 7,
      "outputs": [
        {
          "output_type": "execute_result",
          "data": {
            "text/plain": "Name: My name is John Wick and i worked in a movie called John Wick 4                 \r\nTrimmed: My name is John Wick and i worked in a movie called John Wick 4\r\nLength before: 80, after: 63\r\n"
          },
          "metadata": {},
          "execution_count": 7
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "3fb63c7d-069a-4000-811a-73b2a3c1ebf5",
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": "String name = \"My name is John Wick and i worked in a movie called John Wick 4\";\r\nSystem.out.println(\"Name: \" + name);\r\n\r\n//this is to cut a part out of the string\r\n// Method: substring(beginIndex, endIndex)\r\n// What:   returns the characters from beginIndex up to, but NOT including, endIndex (indexes start at 0)\r\n// Use:    to take a slice of the text, e.g. the first few words\r\nString data = name.substring(0, 15); // indexes 0 to 14 = 15 characters\r\nSystem.out.println(\"Substring: \" + data);",
      "metadata": {
        "language": "java",
        "id": "3fb63c7d-069a-4000-811a-73b2a3c1ebf5",
        "executionSummary": {
          "executionOrder": 15,
          "success": true
        }
      },
      "execution_count": 15,
      "outputs": [
        {
          "output_type": "execute_result",
          "data": {
            "text/plain": "Name: My name is John Wick and i worked in a movie called John Wick 4\r\nSubstring: My name is John\r\n"
          },
          "metadata": {},
          "execution_count": 15
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "f1fd862c-a11e-4c68-a2c4-d4e9c3a6a4c2",
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": "String name = \"My name is John Wick and i worked in a movie called John Wick 4\";\r\nSystem.out.println(\"Name: \" + name);\r\n\r\n//this is to cut the string into pieces\r\n// Method: split(separator)\r\n// What:   returns a String[] array with one piece for every part between the separators\r\n// Use:    to get the single words of a sentence, or the values of a comma-separated line\r\nString[] data = name.split(\" \"); // cut at every space -> 15 words\r\nSystem.out.println(\"Split: \" + Arrays.toString(data)); // Arrays.toString shows the items of an array",
      "metadata": {
        "language": "java",
        "id": "f1fd862c-a11e-4c68-a2c4-d4e9c3a6a4c2",
        "executionSummary": {
